+# Contract: Session-End Signal Request (Host Hook → Runtime)
+
+**Feature**: `001-bench` | **Date**: 2026-10-26
+
+This feature's only external interface is the outbound HTTP request the host hook makes
+when a bound session ends. This file records that request contract — the surface other
+host integrations inheriting this hook, and the consuming Runtime, rely on. Full field
+sources and derivation rules live in [../data-model.md](../data-model.md); this file fixes
+only the observable wire contract.
+
+## Endpoint
+
+```text
+POST {runtime_url}/v1/executions/{execution_id}/signal
+```
+
+- `{runtime_url}` comes from `GRAPHHELM_RUNTIME_URL`; plain `http` must resolve to loopback, otherwise `https`. (Unchanged.)
+- `{execution_id}` comes from `GRAPHHELM_EXECUTION_ID`, URL-quoted with `safe=''`. (Unchanged.)
+
+## Request Headers
+
+| Header | Value | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Authorization` | `Bearer <token from GRAPHHELM_TOKEN_FILE>` | unchanged |
+| `Content-Type` | `application/json` | unchanged |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor` | `{host}-session-{session}` composite actor id | unchanged |
+| `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type` | `agent` | unchanged |
+| `Idempotency-Key` | `session-end-v2-` + first 24 hex chars of the receipt digest | unchanged |
+| **`X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session`** | **validated session id — byte-for-byte equal to `session_id` from the end payload after `_session()` validation (i.e., the session component of `X-GraphHelm-Actor`)** | **NEW** |
+
+Notes on the new header:
+
+- Present on **every** delivery attempt of an undelivered observation, including retries
+  after a refused or mismatching acknowledgment; absent from every other request the hook
+  makes (in particular all start-of-session requests carry no such header).
+- Sent only after session identity validation succeeds; the hook refuses before sending
+  any request when the binding declares a different or missing session id, so a partial or
+  guessed value cannot reach the wire.
+- Request metadata only: it does not enter the signal body, does not change the
+  `Idempotency-Key`, and changes no persisted state.
+- Case: the hook spells the field `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session`; the transport normalizes
+  casing on the wire (`X-Graphhelm-Actor-Session`, measured), matching the treatment of the
+  sibling headers. Field names are case-insensitive for the consumer.
+- Backward compatibility: a Runtime that does not recognize the field completes delivery
+  identically — same acknowledgment body, same delivered marking, same number of requests.
+
+## Request Body
+
+Unchanged: compact JSON `{"signal": {...}}` where the signal object is the persisted
+receipt signal of type `agent_session_ended` (id, source `{type: "tool", id: <actor>}`,
+severity `low`, description, evidence `[execution_id]`, emittedAt).
+
+## Response (expected by the hook)
+
+Unchanged: compact JSON object with `"ok": true` and
+`"data": {"executionId": <same execution id>, "signalId": <same signal id>}`; any other
+shape (or non-2xx/size limits) leaves the observation undelivered and retryable.
