+# Data Model: Host Session Id on the End-of-Session Signal
+
+**Feature**: `001-bench` | **Date**: 2026-10-26 | **Plan**: [plan.md](plan.md)
+
+## Overview
+
+This feature does **not** introduce, rename, or version any persisted entity. It adds one
+request-metadata field to an existing outbound request. The entities below describe that
+request and the surrounding, unchanged identities.
+
+## Entities
+
+### 1. End-of-session observation request *(modified)*
+
+The HTTP POST the host hook sends to the Runtime when a bound session ends.
+
+| Field | Kind | Source | Change in this feature |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Method | `POST` | fixed in `_end_impl()` | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| Endpoint | `{runtime_url}/v1/executions/{execution}/signal` | `binding()` + execution id | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| Body | `{"signal": <signal object>}` compact JSON | persisted delivery receipt | unchanged byte-for-byte (FR-003) |
+| Header `Authorization` | `Bearer <token>` | token file, read per request | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| Header `Content-Type` | `application/json` | added by `request()` when a body exists | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| Header `X-GraphHelm-Actor` | `{host}-session-{session}` | signal source id | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| Header `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type` | `agent` | constant | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| Header `Idempotency-Key` | `session-end-v2-<sha256 digest [:24]>` | deterministic from execution/session/host/origin | unchanged (FR-003) |
+| **Header `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session`** | validated session id, e.g. `session-123` | `_session(payload)` output — identical to the session part of `X-GraphHelm-Actor` | **NEW (FR-001)** |
+
+**Validation rules** (all pre-existing, none modified):
+- The header value is only ever the return of `_session(payload)`: a string fully matching
+  the `ID` pattern `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}` and, if `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID` is set,
+  equal to it. Any failure refuses **before** any request is sent — a partial or guessed
+  session header is structurally impossible.
+- The value equals the session identifier already embedded in `X-GraphHelm-Actor` (FR-002).
+- The header never enters the signal body, never affects the `Idempotency-Key`, and requires
+  no persisted-state change.
+
+### 2. Host session identity *(unchanged)*
+
+- **session id**: from the SessionEnd payload, validated by `_session()`; scopes the state
+  file, the delivery receipt, and the actor identity. No discovery or validation behavior changes.
+
+### 3. Delivery receipt *(unchanged, context)*
+
+Persisted per execution+session+host+origin under the hook state dir; fields
+`{version: 2, executionId, sessionId, host, origin, delivery: {executionId, sessionId, signalId, signal, declaredNodeId, delivered}}`.
+
+**State transition** (unchanged): `delivery.delivered: false → true` after a matching
+acknowledgment. Retries while `delivered == false` rebuild the request from the stored
+receipt plus the freshly validated `session`, so the new header repeats with the same value
+on every attempt (FR-005).
+
+## Relationships
+
+```text
+SessionEnd payload --_session()--> session id (validated)
+                                      |  \
+                                      |   \---> {host}-session-{session} = X-GraphHelm-Actor (unchanged)
+                                      v
+                              X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session (NEW, same value)
+Host binding (env) --> execution id --> endpoint + Idempotency-Key (unchanged)
+State file (delivery receipt) --> signal body + signalId (unchanged bytes)
+```
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+- The Runtime-side presence record that consumes the header (explicitly out of scope in the spec).
+- Start-of-session requests — they gain no header (FR-004, SC-003).
