+# Implementation Plan: Host Session Id on the End-of-Session Signal
+
+**Branch**: `main` (stage setup; no dedicated branch created — the local checkout is the source of truth) | **Date**: 2026-10-26 | **Spec**: [specs/001-bench/spec.md](spec.md)
+
+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-bench/spec.md`
+
+## Summary
+
+When a GraphHelm-bound session ends, `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` posts an
+`agent_session_ended` signal to the Runtime at
+`POST /v1/executions/{execution}/signal` carrying `X-GraphHelm-Actor`,
+`X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type`, and `Idempotency-Key` — but no raw host session id, so the
+Runtime cannot attribute the observation to its originating session. The fix is additive
+and single-site: add one request header, `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session`, set to the already
+validated session id (`_session(payload)` output — the same identifier embedded in the
+actor value `{host}-session-{session}`), at the one place where the end request is built
+(`_end_impl`, the `request(...)` call). The existing end-request contract test
+(`test_end_posts_an_attributed_idempotent_observation_without_success_claim` in
+`plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`) is extended to assert the header's
+presence and exact value; no new helper is introduced, the start path and every existing
+assertion are untouched, and all other hook tests stay green (per Keel, direct route:
+bounded change, two named paths, one observing command).
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: Python 3, stdlib only (the hook already requires 3.8+ idioms such as `str | None` annotations; runs under whatever interpreter the host invokes)
+
+**Primary Dependencies**: None — `urllib.request`, `json`, `hashlib`, `tempfile` stdlib modules already imported by the hook; no new dependency is added
+
+**Storage**: Local per-execution/session JSON state file under `GRAPHHELM_HOOK_STATE_DIR` (or platform default); state format (version 2, delivery receipt) is unchanged by this feature
+
+**Testing**: `unittest` contract suite `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`, driven by an in-process `ThreadingHTTPServer` stand-in Runtime capturing raw request headers — no network, Docker, credentials, or wall-clock assumptions
+
+**Target Platform**: Windows (PowerShell) plus POSIX; the hook is a subprocess CLI invoked by host agent runtimes (`--host claude|codex`)
+
+**Project Type**: CLI host-hook script (plugin boundary under `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/`)
+
+**Performance Goals**: None beyond existing bounds — one loopback/HTTPS POST per undelivered observation, 1.0 s request timeout already enforced in `request()`
+
+**Constraints**: FR-003 — method, endpoint, signal body, idempotency key, and all pre-existing headers of the end request are byte-for-byte unchanged; FR-004 — start-of-session requests gain nothing; task constraint — no new header-helper abstraction, header added inline where the end request is built; header must be stable across retries (FR-005) and must never be sent without a validated session id (mismatched/missing identity still refuses before any request)
